identifier: CHEBI:232425
preferred_term: Sodium glutamate monohydrate
ontology_mapping:
  ontology_id: CHEBI:232425
  ontology_label: monosodium L-glutamate hydrate
  ontology_source: CHEBI
  mapping_quality: EXACT_MATCH
  evidence:
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: CultureMech
    notes: Imported from CultureMech pipeline, quality=DIRECT_MATCH
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: MIM curation (#321)
    notes: molecular_formula 'C5H8NO4.Na' -> 'C5H8NO4.H2O.Na'. The recorded value
      described the anhydrous salt while the label names a hydrate, understating the
      mass by 18 g/mol per water. Corrected because adopted verbatim from the mapped
      term CHEBI:232425 ('monosodium L-glutamate hydrate'), which is the specific
      hydrate and already carries the water.
  - evidence_type: LLM_SUGGESTION
    source: all_unmatched_20261107 worker04 primary proposal glutamate-monohydrate
    notes: NBRC1625 explicitly specifies L-glutamic acid monosodium salt monohydrate;
      CHEBI:232425 provides its one-water formula, InChI and SMILES. Preserve that
      supported structure repair and explicit L alias. DSMZ1454 and JCM904 name sodium
      glutamate monohydrate; their conventional association follows MAPPING_SEMANTICS
      §3, rather than independent supplier proof from automatically matched CAS or
      mass. Neither name-level source association certifies a purchased batch’s enantiomeric
      purity or crystal phase. CH-05 rejects the two water-free systematic aliases
      while preserving their exact text/source. All source-specific, role and whole-owner/export
      holds remain.
